  "claim_short": "Counterexample to the proposed weighted dyadic relaxation in the q-variation context after Theorem 3.3(2) of arXiv:2404.01893. On the one-point space take A=I. Build a bounded smooth multiplier from sine waves of frequencies K_j=2^j supported near log-dyadic centers N_j=2^(6j). Its localized W_2^4 costs are O(K_j^4), so after division by 1+|n| the sum is bounded by C sum K_j^4/N_j=C sum 2^(-2j). On each core block...",
